There are several types of dagger and several monster types that
get daggers in their inventories.  There is one type of javelin and
no monster gets one in their inventory.  This makes daggers
common from the first few levels on and javelins rare throughout
the game.  So I'd use those two javelins until I have four daggers.

Actually my common strategy is to have "a dozen" daggers.  I
will consider other items to substitute for daggers until I have a
dozen daggers then I will start ditching those other items in
favor of daggers.  Later I'll ditch the various dagger types in
favor of better types until I end up with a dozen highly enchanted
daggers.  If I get a knife early on I'll use it for throwing until I
get enough daggers.  Per your discussion here if I get a spear
or javelin early on I'll consider it two daggers and ditch it when
enough daggers arrive.  But given the chance to #enhance
javelin, I'll only do that if I'm convinced I'll never need that slot
for better stuff later.

The common-ness of daggers makes them that much more
valuable over and above their other advantages.  If one javelin
is worth two daggers per throw, there's still the issue that a
nice stack of daggers is assured by well before Medusa but
even a third javelin is not.

